WEBVTT

00:08.508 --> 00:10.760
<i>The True Demon King has died.</i>

00:12.012 --> 00:15.765
<i>The enemy of the world
that filled the horizon with fear,</i>

00:15.765 --> 00:17.684
<i>was defeated by somebody.</i>

00:18.560 --> 00:20.812
<i>To this very day,</i>

00:20.812 --> 00:23.940
<i>that lone Hero remains unknown,
both in name and existence.</i>

00:24.482 --> 00:27.360
<i>Now the age of fear has come to an end,</i>

00:27.652 --> 00:30.947
<i>that person has to be chosen.</i>

00:45.587 --> 00:49.007
ISHURA

02:03.039 --> 02:04.916
Episode 5

02:04.916 --> 02:06.918
Higuare the Pelagic
and Nastique the Quiet Singer

02:06.918 --> 02:09.671
Central Citadel of Lithia

02:10.296 --> 02:11.881
Shalk the Sound Slicer.

02:11.881 --> 02:13.299
Higuare the Pelagic.

02:13.883 --> 02:18.721
You did very well to secure
these two prestigious names, Lana.

02:19.055 --> 02:20.557
Thank you, Master Taren.

02:21.141 --> 02:22.142
However,

02:22.142 --> 02:24.811
it seems finding the World Word
was asking a bit too much.

02:25.562 --> 02:28.398
Surely that's just a rumor
that's been blown out of proportion.

02:28.731 --> 02:31.067
If someone with almighty Word Arts
really existed,

02:31.067 --> 02:33.319
they could easily win any war.

02:33.319 --> 02:35.864
Say they do exist,

02:35.864 --> 02:39.576
we'd have to think of a way
to control them.

02:40.160 --> 02:41.703
I've heard rumors of you too,

02:41.703 --> 02:43.121
Higuare the Pelagic.

02:44.414 --> 02:47.542
You never lost once when you fought
as a Gladiator in the remote regions.

02:47.542 --> 02:48.626
That's right.

02:48.626 --> 02:51.421
I fought for a fairly long time.

02:51.421 --> 02:53.173
In minian years,

02:53.173 --> 02:55.800
it would be 13 or 14 years.

02:56.134 --> 02:57.844
A slave Gladiator?

02:57.844 --> 03:01.347
There are barbaric cities
in the remote regions that place bets

03:01.347 --> 03:03.183
on the lives of people and beasts.

03:03.183 --> 03:05.518
Of course,
this practice is illegal.

03:05.810 --> 03:07.854
In the era of the True Demon King,

03:07.854 --> 03:10.690
many places must have
slipped past the reach of the kingdom.

03:10.690 --> 03:12.859
Something doesn't sound
right here.

03:13.443 --> 03:17.238
Some slave traders
bossed you around for 14 years,

03:17.947 --> 03:20.491
yet you're supposed
to be invincible or something?

03:21.075 --> 03:22.869
He has a point.

03:23.328 --> 03:25.705
Would you care to provide an explanation,

03:25.705 --> 03:26.789
Higuare?

03:27.373 --> 03:28.791
As you wish.

03:29.417 --> 03:31.878
<i>I was born in the far west,</i>

03:31.878 --> 03:33.796
<i>in a place unknown to the minian races.</i>

03:33.796 --> 03:35.006
Here they are!

03:35.006 --> 03:36.216
Mandrakes!

03:36.925 --> 03:38.760
This will be a huge haul.

03:46.935 --> 03:49.020
What am I to do here?

03:49.020 --> 03:50.396
Isn't it obvious?

03:50.396 --> 03:52.357
You're to fight.

03:52.690 --> 03:53.983
Fight?

03:53.983 --> 03:57.403
Simply killing a defenseless mandrake

03:57.403 --> 03:59.030
won't get the crowd going.

04:07.205 --> 04:08.623
I understand.

04:08.623 --> 04:09.916
I will fight.

04:10.583 --> 04:11.876
Fight!

04:11.876 --> 04:14.295
- Make a move!
- Kill that thing!

04:53.543 --> 04:56.254
Who am I to fight
in the next match?

04:56.254 --> 04:58.589
Three high-ranking fighters.

04:58.589 --> 05:00.550
Put on a good show when you die.

05:01.009 --> 05:02.093
Die?

05:02.093 --> 05:04.304
What is the meaning of that word?

05:04.304 --> 05:06.639
I'm sorry to tell you this, Higuare,

05:07.140 --> 05:10.643
but in this arena,
you either kill, or you die.

05:12.103 --> 05:13.313
Kill

05:13.313 --> 05:14.480
or die?

05:28.745 --> 05:30.830
Kill or die.

05:35.501 --> 05:38.338
I'm selling you to another city.

05:38.963 --> 05:42.884
Will I be made to fight
even stronger opponents?

05:43.301 --> 05:44.344
That's right.

05:44.344 --> 05:46.596
The crowd wants to see you get killed.

05:47.388 --> 05:50.892
It simply looks more spectacular
when the minian races defeat the monster.

05:51.517 --> 05:54.020
Am I to die?

05:54.604 --> 05:56.814
Well, probably.

05:59.650 --> 06:00.735
No.

06:00.735 --> 06:02.653
I do not wish to die.

06:05.198 --> 06:07.450
- Kill it!
- You can do it!

06:09.827 --> 06:11.662
<i>In addition to hip rotation,</i>

06:11.662 --> 06:14.665
<i>they use their spines
to increase the speed of their thrusts.</i>

06:14.665 --> 06:16.501
<i>To recreate that movement,</i>

06:16.501 --> 06:18.711
<i>I'll twist my fibrovascular bundles together.</i>

06:26.177 --> 06:28.763
<i>I might match him in speed,
but he beats me in strength.</i>

06:29.180 --> 06:31.015
<i>But if I use my vine arms...</i>

06:34.268 --> 06:36.479
<i>Check the muscles of the fingers.</i>

06:37.063 --> 06:40.358
<i>Will my slash attack reach
before the bullets are fired?</i>

06:40.858 --> 06:43.945
<i>Perhaps if I disappear from view
using the recoil from a vine shot...</i>

06:45.655 --> 06:47.782
Who will I be fighting next?

06:47.782 --> 06:51.536
You've now made your name
as the strongest Gladiator there is.

06:51.536 --> 06:52.995
Not a single spectator

06:52.995 --> 06:55.665
is wishing for the fall
of Higuare the Pelagic.

06:56.290 --> 06:58.126
If I don't keep up my training,

06:58.126 --> 07:00.461
I might be defeated eventually.

07:01.546 --> 07:04.382
For an invincible slave,
you're not much fun.

07:12.723 --> 07:14.767
<i>Do I wish to keep living?</i>

07:16.436 --> 07:18.187
<i>What would be the meaning</i>

07:18.563 --> 07:19.981
<i>in living on like this?</i>

07:21.482 --> 07:23.734
<i>It's not like I'm fixated with life.</i>

07:25.278 --> 07:26.279
<i>I just...</i>

07:27.196 --> 07:28.698
<i>don't wish to die.</i>

07:33.661 --> 07:35.329
Come on! You're fighting too!

07:35.329 --> 07:36.747
Has something happened?

07:36.747 --> 07:38.291
The Demon King!

07:38.291 --> 07:40.209
The army of the True Demon King!

07:57.143 --> 07:58.728
Shoot. They're running riot.

08:12.825 --> 08:14.160
I see.

08:14.160 --> 08:16.287
It's kill or die.

08:23.085 --> 08:25.838
I've killed so many up to now.

08:29.342 --> 08:33.095
After all that,
I won't be killed by this level of enemy.

08:36.557 --> 08:37.558
<i>I see.</i>

08:37.558 --> 08:40.061
<i>This is what they call pride.</i>

08:56.285 --> 08:57.453
When I found him,

08:57.453 --> 09:00.122
they told me he'd been slaying
the Demon King's army.

09:00.122 --> 09:03.960
I've never heard of anybody
who would charge head first

09:03.960 --> 09:05.628
right into the Demon King's army.

09:05.628 --> 09:07.088
Hm?

09:07.797 --> 09:09.298
Mm. Oh.

09:09.298 --> 09:10.466
Oh, Miss Taren.

09:11.133 --> 09:14.220
It seems we have more
unusual guests today too.

09:14.220 --> 09:16.430
Introduce yourself, Dakai.

09:17.139 --> 09:19.308
Is that skeleton a spear wielder?

09:19.308 --> 09:21.060
The name's Shalk the Sound Slicer.

09:21.686 --> 09:23.312
As for the mandrake,

09:23.312 --> 09:26.357
well, he seems like
an unpredictable fellow.

09:26.357 --> 09:29.360
I can't even tell where your face is.

09:29.360 --> 09:31.737
My name is Higuare the Pelagic.

09:31.737 --> 09:32.822
Nice to meet you.

09:33.739 --> 09:36.325
<i>It looks like a normal knife.</i>

09:36.325 --> 09:38.703
<i>He probably has several
hidden in his body.</i>

09:39.287 --> 09:42.081
Both are strong and trustworthy fighters,
just like yourself.

09:42.623 --> 09:45.042
Much like the True Demon King,

09:45.042 --> 09:48.838
I believe we require unique powers
that fill enemy armies with dread.

09:48.838 --> 09:51.340
Feeling up to that task, Shalk?

09:51.340 --> 09:55.094
Sorry, but unlike Higuare,
I'm a mercenary.

09:55.386 --> 09:58.097
Until I receive my reward in advance,

09:58.097 --> 10:00.433
working would be
a breach of my principles.

10:00.433 --> 10:02.143
I know that.

10:02.143 --> 10:06.063
The reward you're after
is information on the Final Land

10:06.063 --> 10:07.690
where the True Demon King died, right?

10:07.690 --> 10:09.900
Mm. Hm?

10:11.152 --> 10:12.403
I know your trick.

10:12.403 --> 10:15.114
You get your reward
and then run off, don't you?

10:15.114 --> 10:16.449
And I know yours.

10:16.449 --> 10:20.119
You thought I'd work for free
just because I'm dead, right?

10:20.703 --> 10:21.704
Not bad.

10:21.704 --> 10:23.998
I don't dislike someone
who knows how to talk.

10:24.582 --> 10:26.959
You, on the other hand,
are strangely quiet.

10:26.959 --> 10:29.253
Tell me, what do you usually eat?

10:37.053 --> 10:38.721
I don't eat fruit.

10:41.557 --> 10:42.975
Is that so?

10:42.975 --> 10:45.936
If you wish to see my power,

10:45.936 --> 10:47.730
then you've just seen it.

10:49.523 --> 10:50.566
Splendid.

10:50.566 --> 10:52.818
Unbelievable skill.

10:52.818 --> 10:56.280
So that means mandrakes
can use three arms at once?

10:56.280 --> 10:57.865
- Not quite...
- Huh?

11:04.830 --> 11:07.583
I can use 42 arms.

11:08.250 --> 11:11.712
<i>He is the one whose
dueling skills have been honed</i>

11:11.712 --> 11:13.631
<i>through immense bloodshed.</i>

11:15.383 --> 11:19.095
<i>The one who harbors
an absolute and lethal poison,</i>

11:19.095 --> 11:21.639
<i>that no living thing can stop.</i>

11:22.973 --> 11:25.893
<i>The one who boasts
infinitely brilliant swordplay,</i>

11:25.893 --> 11:29.605
<i>perfected by his bizarre physique.</i>

11:30.856 --> 11:34.944
<i>He obeys all, yet is ruled by none.</i>

11:35.528 --> 11:38.072
<i>A most free slave.</i>

11:43.911 --> 11:48.374
<i>He is a Gladiator. He is a mandrake.
He is Higuare the Pelagic.</i>

11:49.041 --> 11:52.962
Ishura
Mandrake

11:55.715 --> 11:59.218
Raishi Mountain Village

12:02.805 --> 12:05.474
All this luggage
is really slowing us down.

12:05.474 --> 12:08.144
It will probably take
three and a half days from here.

12:08.144 --> 12:09.979
- Huh?
- Kuze.

12:09.979 --> 12:12.523
Are there enough beds for the whole squad?

12:12.523 --> 12:13.941
If beds are all we need,

12:13.941 --> 12:16.527
the Religious Order's poorhouse
has spare rooms.

12:16.527 --> 12:17.945
But I'm not sure about food...

12:17.945 --> 12:20.489
You won't catch my soldiers
begging for food from the Order.

12:20.489 --> 12:22.241
How pathetic.

12:22.241 --> 12:25.494
They say you're a cleanup guy
for the Religious Order,

12:25.494 --> 12:27.329
but are you really strong?

12:28.497 --> 12:29.999
Well, of course, I am.

12:33.544 --> 12:36.255
Because I have an angel by my side.

12:38.674 --> 12:41.594
Mr. Kuze, how many years has it been?

12:41.594 --> 12:43.679
I've come back, Ripel.

12:43.679 --> 12:46.891
And I've brought a lot of guests.
Sorry about this.

12:47.933 --> 12:49.101
Good evening.

12:49.101 --> 12:50.519
Nice to meet you.

12:50.519 --> 12:53.522
Let's see... you must be Ripel.

12:53.522 --> 12:54.648
Yes.

12:54.648 --> 12:56.942
My second name is Ripel the Frost Leaf.

12:56.942 --> 12:58.778
Um, who are you?

12:59.361 --> 13:01.113
Nihilo the Vortical Stampede.

13:01.655 --> 13:03.699
Kuze is my escort.

13:04.408 --> 13:05.409
Escort?

13:05.409 --> 13:07.161
For a girl like her?

13:07.161 --> 13:09.622
I'm her escort, nothing more.

13:10.748 --> 13:12.458
I know.

13:12.458 --> 13:15.878
Mr. Kuze, you never did have much luck
with the ladies.

13:17.421 --> 13:20.508
Oh, boy, is it really that obvious?

13:21.091 --> 13:23.093
I'll go get changed.

13:25.763 --> 13:27.264
She's a good girl.

13:27.264 --> 13:30.309
She didn't ask about my body.

13:30.309 --> 13:33.562
I heard you were being held prisoner.

13:33.562 --> 13:36.565
Did you get out
because you made up for your crimes?

13:36.565 --> 13:37.775
Nope.

13:37.775 --> 13:41.987
I simply promised to help Hidow,
in exchange for my release.

13:41.987 --> 13:45.950
Then, what if you never made that promise?

13:45.950 --> 13:47.368
Who knows?

13:47.368 --> 13:49.703
I might have fought my way out.

13:49.703 --> 13:51.622
I was created to fight, after all.

13:52.331 --> 13:53.541
What about you, Kuze?

13:53.958 --> 13:55.876
I'm not the fighting type.

13:56.919 --> 13:59.421
You don't carry a weapon, do you?

13:59.421 --> 14:02.424
You look like you're scared
of hurting another person.

14:02.883 --> 14:04.009
Come on now.

14:04.009 --> 14:06.512
Don't bully this weak, old man too much.

14:07.137 --> 14:09.265
Still, you're just like me.

14:09.265 --> 14:12.476
You survived the era
of the True Demon King.

14:12.476 --> 14:15.271
It's nothing to brag about.

14:16.313 --> 14:18.357
I have an angel by my side.

14:18.357 --> 14:20.192
That's why I survived.

14:20.192 --> 14:21.277
That's all.

14:22.027 --> 14:23.237
Hmm...

14:25.072 --> 14:26.407
Amazing!

14:26.407 --> 14:27.491
Wow!

14:27.491 --> 14:28.868
It's made with sheep's milk!

14:28.868 --> 14:30.786
I heard we're getting this
thanks to Mr. Kuze.

14:30.786 --> 14:32.246
Quiet down.

14:32.246 --> 14:34.498
You'll talk the food off the table.

14:35.583 --> 14:38.335
I feel terrible.
You didn't have to do all this.

14:38.335 --> 14:39.712
It's no problem.

14:39.712 --> 14:42.464
Churches everywhere
help each other out these days.

14:42.965 --> 14:44.550
This was all so sudden,

14:44.550 --> 14:47.553
but you did well to prepare rooms
for all the merchants.

14:47.553 --> 14:48.637
Well,

14:49.096 --> 14:53.392
a little while back,
soldiers from Aureatia camped here.

14:53.392 --> 14:54.768
Soldiers from Aureatia?

14:54.768 --> 14:56.645
The merchants you brought today

14:56.645 --> 14:59.356
are a lot more polite
than the soldiers from Aureatia.

14:59.356 --> 15:01.275
They're actually helping me out.

15:01.859 --> 15:03.527
Why did those soldiers come here?

15:03.527 --> 15:05.613
Soldiers under the command
of Sir Harghent,

15:05.613 --> 15:08.157
the Sixth General
of the Twenty-Nine Officials of Aureatia

15:08.741 --> 15:11.368
said they were going to defeat
that Vikeon the Smoldering.

15:12.036 --> 15:13.120
Vikeon?

15:13.120 --> 15:15.331
A black dragon from the age of legends.

15:15.331 --> 15:16.457
Roar!

15:17.041 --> 15:18.125
My name is Vikeon!

15:18.125 --> 15:19.209
Be very afraid!

15:19.793 --> 15:21.462
If we're playing dragon hunting,

15:21.462 --> 15:23.797
shouldn't I play
the role of Vikeon the Smoldering?

15:23.797 --> 15:24.924
Then who am I?

15:24.924 --> 15:26.800
You're Rosclay the Absolute.

15:27.384 --> 15:29.345
Here I come.

15:30.679 --> 15:32.473
I won't lose!

15:33.265 --> 15:34.767
Not bad!

15:34.767 --> 15:37.478
- Mr. Kuze hasn't changed.
- Huh?

15:37.478 --> 15:39.521
- I'm not done yet!
- Was he always like this?

15:39.521 --> 15:41.732
Yes. He's always been so laid-back.

15:41.732 --> 15:44.109
No grandeur at all.

15:44.109 --> 15:46.946
Even though he has to take on
so many problems with the Religious Order,

15:46.946 --> 15:48.781
he's always laughing.

15:50.240 --> 15:51.575
<i>An angel, huh?</i>

15:56.038 --> 15:58.999
The corridor is the only way
to enter the room.

15:58.999 --> 16:01.961
I'll take a rest on this bench.

16:02.753 --> 16:04.755
As ever the gentleman.

16:04.755 --> 16:07.424
I don't mind you sleeping
in the same room as me.

16:08.509 --> 16:10.928
You mustn't tease an old man.

16:10.928 --> 16:12.513
Go to sleep. You're in safe hands.

16:17.768 --> 16:18.811
Mm.

16:18.811 --> 16:21.146
I'm glad everyone seems well.

16:21.563 --> 16:23.315
It was around four years ago.

16:23.899 --> 16:26.026
I used to live here.

16:26.610 --> 16:28.779
The shoddy window fittings

16:28.779 --> 16:31.407
haven't changed at all.

16:40.249 --> 16:41.667
Ripel?

16:42.668 --> 16:43.711
Mr. Kuze.

16:45.879 --> 16:48.090
Won't you cooperate with Lithia?

16:49.883 --> 16:52.469
After the Sixth General's
soldiers came,

16:52.469 --> 16:55.222
people from Lithia came to investigate.

16:55.973 --> 17:00.769
They said if we help them,
then they would support our church.

17:01.353 --> 17:03.814
I can't fight, but you can, Mr. Kuze.

17:03.814 --> 17:06.150
You're extremely strong, Mr. Kuze.

17:07.776 --> 17:09.028
I see.

17:09.028 --> 17:11.989
I knew I'd caused you pain.

17:11.989 --> 17:13.157
Mr. Kuze?

17:13.741 --> 17:15.492
But I'm sorry, Ripel.

17:16.201 --> 17:18.078
I can't help you.

17:18.078 --> 17:20.456
The way I'd help just won't work.

17:20.956 --> 17:22.541
I really am sorry.

17:22.541 --> 17:23.667
Huh?

17:30.340 --> 17:32.676
Wait! Please don't kill him!

17:32.676 --> 17:34.303
You're in the line of fire!

17:34.303 --> 17:36.388
That man has dealings with Aureatia!

17:37.931 --> 17:41.185
I guess it's the Sixth General and his
pointless antics I have to thank for this.

17:43.812 --> 17:46.398
The world truly is a dangerous place.

17:46.398 --> 17:49.026
The people with you
aren't really merchants, are they?

17:49.026 --> 17:50.486
Kuze the Passing Disaster!

17:56.241 --> 17:57.367
His defense is good.

17:57.367 --> 17:58.660
Give up on taking him alive.

17:58.660 --> 17:59.745
Understood.

18:02.581 --> 18:05.542
I'm begging you, don't kill them.

18:08.170 --> 18:09.546
You're mine now!

18:18.514 --> 18:21.934
I thought I told you not to kill them.

18:21.934 --> 18:24.019
- Poison?
- Maybe a concealed weapon.

18:24.019 --> 18:25.646
Keep your distance and shoot him down!

18:38.659 --> 18:40.994
Just who is this guy?

18:42.204 --> 18:44.289
Didn't you ever learn?

18:44.289 --> 18:47.793
Didn't you take lessons at church
when you were little?

18:47.793 --> 18:49.711
If you do something bad,

18:49.711 --> 18:52.548
you'll be punished by an angel.

19:11.608 --> 19:13.318
He nearly had you there.

19:13.694 --> 19:15.946
Thanks, Nihilo.

19:17.739 --> 19:20.284
I'm sorry, Mr. Kuze.

19:20.284 --> 19:22.744
I never thought they'd try to kill you.

19:23.412 --> 19:25.372
I know.

19:25.372 --> 19:27.666
You didn't do anything wrong, Ripel.

19:28.250 --> 19:30.419
I-I'm sorry.

19:30.419 --> 19:33.172
Ripel, can you show me your stomach?

19:37.718 --> 19:39.511
The kidney has been pierced.

19:40.679 --> 19:43.015
I thought if I could make everyone happy,

19:43.640 --> 19:46.351
then I'd be like you.

19:47.352 --> 19:49.396
Ripel, I'm sorry.

19:50.022 --> 19:51.523
I'm the one who's sorry.

20:13.754 --> 20:17.007
Nihilo, you've died once before
haven't you?

20:17.007 --> 20:18.217
Yeah.

20:18.217 --> 20:21.053
Did you see an angel when you died?

20:21.053 --> 20:22.512
An angel?

20:22.512 --> 20:24.932
I think someone just made them up.

20:25.515 --> 20:26.516
Well,

20:26.516 --> 20:28.727
I think so too.

20:30.020 --> 20:32.481
Even so, angels do exist.

20:42.699 --> 20:45.994
You know, I think angels are lonely too.

20:52.251 --> 20:53.961
This whole time,

20:55.087 --> 20:56.964
were you watching an angel?

20:58.548 --> 20:59.967
Perhaps.

21:00.717 --> 21:03.971
Or maybe it's the angel
who is watching me.

21:03.971 --> 21:07.766
That's why she kills
whoever tries to kill me.

21:08.809 --> 21:10.018
What's her name?

21:10.477 --> 21:11.478
Her name?

21:11.478 --> 21:13.397
The name of your angel.

21:13.814 --> 21:14.940
Right.

21:14.940 --> 21:17.192
I've never told anyone before.

21:17.776 --> 21:18.944
Not even Ripel.

21:19.403 --> 21:20.404
But I do know it.

21:20.404 --> 21:21.738
Her name is...

21:23.448 --> 21:25.867
<i>She is the one who is
undetected by anyone in this world,</i>

21:25.867 --> 21:29.121
<i>except for a single person.</i>

21:29.955 --> 21:33.250
<i>The one who is immune
to interference by any means,</i>

21:33.250 --> 21:36.378
<i>an immaterial consciousness.</i>

21:37.337 --> 21:40.090
<i>The one who, since the dawn of the world,</i>

21:40.090 --> 21:43.760
<i>has possessed
the absolute authority to end life.</i>

21:44.344 --> 21:46.263
<i>But she comes silently,</i>

21:46.263 --> 21:49.516
<i>and takes everything
without ever being seen.</i>

21:49.516 --> 21:52.394
<i>The embodiment of the fate of death.</i>

21:56.273 --> 21:58.191
The name of my angel is...

22:00.736 --> 22:02.821
<i>She is a Stabber.
She is an angel.</i>

22:02.821 --> 22:05.198
<i>She is Nastique the Quiet Singer.</i>

23:36.331 --> 23:38.333
Translated by Zacarias Hicks

23:39.334 --> 23:41.044
Episode 6
Gathering of Factions
